                        ],
                        "form": "ancre-charrues"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "3da4070d-602f-4d79-805e-296ee97eae6f",
                        "entry_id": "4cffab09-9b68-3cbe-bd9b-a5ddbf61a570",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "ancre à soc de charrue"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b60c8706-e3b3-357a-af07-2724149adad1",
                        "entry_id": "4cffab09-9b68-3cbe-bd9b-a5ddbf61a570",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ancre de conception moderne (XXᵉ siècle), composée de deux lames symétriques incurvées, rappelant chacune un soc de charrue, soudées ensemble, et surmontées d’une verge, articulée ou fixe, quasiment horizontale. Lorsqu’une traction est exercée sur l’extrémité de la verge, l’ancre s’enfouit dans le substrat à la manière d’une charrue."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9a4a732-a018-408c-bd82-2b751e4b41f6",
                                "sense_id": "b60c8706-e3b3-357a-af07-2724149adad1",
                                "text": "En plongeant, aujourd’hui, j’ai vérifié que la vase se dépose uniquement au fond des baies ou dans les endroits sans courant, son épaisseur atteint rarement plus de 20 centimètres. Au-dessous, j’ai retrouvé la roche, polie par la glace. Il est illusoire d’espérer une tenue correcte du mouillage dans de tels sols. À la limite, cette fine couche de vase rend le glissement encore plus facile. Nous avons essayé d’empenneler une ancre-charrue de 35 kilos sur notre F.O.B. de 45 kilos, suivie de 60 mètres de chaîne, en 12 millimètres. En tout, 350 kilos de ferraille, Dans moins de 10 mètres d’eau, le moteur en marche arrière, nous les avons facilement faire déraper. Et pourtant 350 kilos, c’est lourd ; très lourd, même, lorsque nous les remontons avec un guindeau manuel."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "895196c4-4ccb-4a24-93a7-0b41a571ae10",
                        "source_entry_id": "4cffab09-9b68-3cbe-bd9b-a5ddbf61a570",
                        "source_sense_id": "b60c8706-e3b3-357a-af07-2724149adad1",
                        "target_lang_word": "plough",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "plough",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f847eba6-8bd6-3bbe-b310-69690310621b",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5c6d99-c484-3478-91b3-8b42ef13ee10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A device pulled through the ground in order to break it open into furrows for planting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab48fd22-fa6f-49c7-aec9-f48ac2c79407",
                                                "sense_id": "f847eba6-8bd6-3bbe-b310-69690310621b",
                                                "text": "The horse-drawn plough had a tremendous impact on agriculture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0086ef21-959c-4b9c-b102-33f6debeb375",
                                                "sense_id": "f847eba6-8bd6-3bbe-b310-69690310621b",
                                                "text": "Meronyms: ploughshare, plowshare, share, moldboard, mouldboard, coulter, colter, jointer, chisel, ploughbeam, beam, ploughstaff, staff, hake"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8677472a-a89c-4698-9d71-93b0cf165603",
                                                "sense_id": "f847eba6-8bd6-3bbe-b310-69690310621b",
                                                "text": "The central theme of low-till agriculture is that the plough is not always necessary and that it should be used only when truly appropriate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e61b3a2c-0b33-3d2e-a18d-7cde61370ed0",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5c6d99-c484-3478-91b3-8b42ef13ee10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several other tools or implements that cut and push material.",
                                            "Ellipsis of snowplough."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd02a192-6e09-4e36-b025-6cbba91804d3",
                                                "sense_id": "e61b3a2c-0b33-3d2e-a18d-7cde61370ed0",
                                                "text": "It's been three hours since a plough came through here, and now you can hardly even tell that it did! [the snow keeps falling heavily]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3795fefc-b21e-31ce-b4f4-56fa6087a0ee",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5c6d99-c484-3478-91b3-8b42ef13ee10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several other tools or implements that cut and push material.",
                                            "A joiner's plane for making grooves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "90c17e3e-ced2-3bdd-9d8a-5e422ef1c63b",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5c6d99-c484-3478-91b3-8b42ef13ee10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of several other tools or implements that cut and push material.",
                                            "A bookbinder's implement for trimming or shaving off the edges of books."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0f90bdc-a2f2-3c0f-bfe7-6ad2498cdd31",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5c6d99-c484-3478-91b3-8b42ef13ee10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The use of a plough; tillage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2eaa95cc-5c7e-40da-a1ff-b70b5a50f58e",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f90bdc-a2f2-3c0f-bfe7-6ad2498cdd31",
                                                "text": "If you get it early ploughed and it lies all winter possibly, you find it an advantage to give it a second plough; but it does not invariably follow that we plough twice for our green crop."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e6e86b8-c72b-372f-b507-a91a8b008fb9",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5c6d99-c484-3478-91b3-8b42ef13ee10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of Plough (Synonym of Ursa Major)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3d641cf-a547-41eb-84f2-d10d00d25af3",
                                                "sense_id": "1e6e86b8-c72b-372f-b507-a91a8b008fb9",
                                                "text": "Rising in the north-east fairly high in the sky, Arcturus may be found by following round the curve of the plough."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "395931b8-b4b4-4cea-a84e-01ece2201175",
                                                "sense_id": "1e6e86b8-c72b-372f-b507-a91a8b008fb9",
                                                "text": "To many generations of rice farmers in rural Java, Indonesia, it was not the stars of Ursa Major that formed the plough, but the stars of Orion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6643abd-ef9b-4e6d-b599-3d7cbb3c0a86",
                                                "sense_id": "1e6e86b8-c72b-372f-b507-a91a8b008fb9",
                                                "text": "Across the Atlantic, what we call the Big Dipper has been called many other names. In England, this grouping of stars is seen as the plough."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fa08129-1f04-4944-a093-79d8c809c9a5",
                                                "sense_id": "1e6e86b8-c72b-372f-b507-a91a8b008fb9",
                                                "text": "Consider the Big Dipper, or as it is also known, the plough or the wagon."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1ad3c6e-9970-3830-8708-6e315bcfc7a2",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5c6d99-c484-3478-91b3-8b42ef13ee10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of ploughland, an alternative name for a carucate or hide."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee4431f1-9427-43c6-ae8b-dc3d4ff4eb35",
                                                "sense_id": "d1ad3c6e-9970-3830-8708-6e315bcfc7a2",
                                                "text": "c. 1350, Geoffrey Chaucer (attributed), The Tale of Gamelyn\nJohan, mine eldest son, shall have plowes five."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "14ff7941-3c2c-397b-8ff9-b1ed2f7e4d42",
                                        "entry_id": "5f5c6d99-c484-3478-91b3-8b42ef13ee10",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A yoga pose resembling a traditional plough, halāsana."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plough",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cd04433-c2e9-33ad-9483-4712ed118b46",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use a plough on soil to prepare for planting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "beccfa23-8092-45c7-93e7-b35686a4c610",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd04433-c2e9-33ad-9483-4712ed118b46",
                                                "text": "I've still got to plough that field."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e26f5e6-3925-42aa-aba5-4e909aae9cc7",
                                                "sense_id": "0cd04433-c2e9-33ad-9483-4712ed118b46",
                                                "text": "That there is and from time immemorial has been within that part of the parish called Mablethorpe St. Mary's a laudable custom that, if any outdweller take ancient pasture ground, he shall pay a modus of 4d. an acre, and so in proportion, on the 1st of August, in lieu of all manner of tithe; and that if any of the ancient pasture be once ploughed up or meadowed, it shall, when restored to pasture again, pay 4d. the acre in the hands of such outdweller."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c407550-f12e-36ff-88e0-fac217dc5b06",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use a plough."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f2bf762-498b-49c0-aa90-c4a58f3e7a75",
                                                "sense_id": "9c407550-f12e-36ff-88e0-fac217dc5b06",
                                                "text": "Some days I have to plough from sunrise to sunset."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa0f8d18-9e9a-30b1-8276-5ed0e587c1f8",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move with force."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f59e711-86cd-45eb-8d8e-e557ceef2b83",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0f8d18-9e9a-30b1-8276-5ed0e587c1f8",
                                                "text": "Trucks ploughed through the water to ferry flood victims to safety."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be1cb71b-0b0d-4e86-9377-5f88e3b934c9",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0f8d18-9e9a-30b1-8276-5ed0e587c1f8",
                                                "text": "Wolves continued to plough forward as young Belgian midfielder Mujangi Bia and Ronald Zubar both hit shots wide from good positions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7da7c1cf-7bb2-4f5a-b284-d3cfe81f0f89",
                                                "sense_id": "fa0f8d18-9e9a-30b1-8276-5ed0e587c1f8",
                                                "text": "Thirteen people were injured in August 1957 when this Bristol freighter skidded on the runway at Southend Airport when landing with a flight from Calais. It ploughed through the boundary fence, but thankfully stopped short of the railway and the 1,500V overhead wires. A tripwire was installed on this section of Shenfield-Southend line to warn train drivers of instances such as this."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3a152267-3992-3be3-ae1e-456d005e7247",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To knock over or run over (someone) without stopping."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15beabe6-09ac-49ad-9add-b256ed9d28f7",
                                                "sense_id": "3a152267-3992-3be3-ae1e-456d005e7247",
                                                "text": "My brother ploughed me over."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "971ea88c-172c-46a1-93cb-b4391f96ca41",
                                                "sense_id": "3a152267-3992-3be3-ae1e-456d005e7247",
                                                "text": "Three people were ploughed down when he lost control of the truck."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9ea2e61c-7570-3c61-8d4c-ba112c506a5c",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To furrow; to make furrows, grooves, or ridges in."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb2c96fc-3eec-4604-a341-b6847b5baf17",
                                                "sense_id": "9ea2e61c-7570-3c61-8d4c-ba112c506a5c",
                                                "text": "Let patient Octavia plough thy visage up / With her prepared nails."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61f9a112-6e94-3872-a432-cf59a5c328a6",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To run through, as in sailing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5437685c-bab3-41eb-ba3d-1dbd6edb6cb8",
                                                "sense_id": "61f9a112-6e94-3872-a432-cf59a5c328a6",
                                                "text": "With speed we plough the watery way."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af21fa7d-5468-3320-893a-f4c22e73935e",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To trim, or shave off the edges of, as a book or paper, with a plough."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0db0f784-bccc-3d71-8796-7c16609034b2",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cut a groove in, as in a plank, or the edge of a board; especially, a rectangular groove to receive the end of a shelf or tread, the edge of a panel, a tongue, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "984cfdf1-9b19-3392-a9d6-5d6a34ad6392",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To fail (a student)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d127e405-9ac1-4273-a973-c08cfff920d7",
                                                "sense_id": "984cfdf1-9b19-3392-a9d6-5d6a34ad6392",
                                                "text": "The good Professor scolded, predicted that they would all be either gulfed or ploughed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83f10ed7-bb00-4a83-9500-92d5487aacb4",
                                                "sense_id": "984cfdf1-9b19-3392-a9d6-5d6a34ad6392",
                                                "text": "You see, Miss Dodd, an university examination consists of several items: neglect but one, and Crichton himself would be ploughed; because brilliancy in your other papers is not allowed to count; that is how the most distinguished man of our day got ploughed for Smalls."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba61fbc3-8011-426b-a82f-be1af090bac6",
                                                "sense_id": "984cfdf1-9b19-3392-a9d6-5d6a34ad6392",
                                                "text": "I knew one of that lot at Corpus; in fact, we were crammed by the same tutor for \"smalls,\" and both got ploughed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e63b225a-135f-3adf-a557-b6551a1d4a8c",
                                        "entry_id": "2e4a6a9a-b05b-31a1-b6a1-7dcc9dbf1f73",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To sexually penetrate, typically in a vigorous manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78bc7329-ac3e-4e6f-9996-ed46b6bb448a",
                                                "sense_id": "e63b225a-135f-3adf-a557-b6551a1d4a8c",
                                                "text": "I love just getting ploughed face down on my bed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f544ba0-0b72-4f2a-85f1-60450579cb48",
                                                "sense_id": "e63b225a-135f-3adf-a557-b6551a1d4a8c",
                                                "text": "If you don't use rubbers when you're plowing someone's throat, don't bother answering this ad."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
